Carafe Lab: process page traversal uses the page type to determine whether a page is mapped.
The address field contains physical minus virtual address, so zero is valid for an identity
mapping. Treating zero as unmapped made MapProcessCodeMemory reject valid heap backing with
InvalidCurrentMemory, preventing Carbon's ASI modules from loading.
GPL-3.0-or-later, as the file it changes.

--- a/src/common/page_table.cpp
+++ b/src/common/page_table.cpp
@@ -26,7 +26,7 @@
     // Validate that we can read the actual entry.
     if (auto const page = context->next_page; page < entries.size()) {
         // Validate that the entry is mapped.
-        if (auto const paddr = entries[page].addr; paddr != 0) {
+        if (auto const paddr = entries[page].addr; entries[page].ptr.Type() != PageType::Unmapped) {
             // Populate the results.
             out_entry->phys_addr = paddr + context->next_offset;
             context->next_page += 1;
